,"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout","abstract":[{"text":"A system is a group of staves that are read and played simultaneously. System layout includes left and right","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"margins and the vertical distance from the previous system. The system distance is measured from the bottom","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"line of the previous system to the top line of the current system. It is ignored for the first system on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"page. The top system distance is measured from the page’s top margin to the top line of the first system. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ignored for all but the first system on a page.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemDividers":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLSystemDividers","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemDividers","abstract":[{"text":"The system-dividers element indicates the presence or absence of system dividers (also known as system","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"separation marks) between systems displayed on the same page. Dividers on the left and right side of the page","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are controlled by the left-divider and right-divider elements respectively. The default vertical position is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"half the system-distance value from the top of the system that is below the divider. The default horizontal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position is the left and right system margin, respectively.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemDividers","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemDividers","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemdividers"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout/systemDividers":{"type":"topic","title":"systemDividers","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout\/systemDividers","abstract":[{"text":"The presence or absence of system dividers between this system and the previous system.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"systemDividers","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemDividers","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemDividersV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout\/systemdividers"}}}